CowSwapModuleFactory_Create
├── when owner is zero address
│   └── it should revert with CowSwapModuleFactory_ZeroOwner
├── when paymentRails is zero address
│   └── it should revert with CowSwapModuleFactory_ZeroPaymentRails
├── when paymentRails is an EOA
│   └── it should revert with CowSwapModuleFactory_PaymentRailsNotContract
├── when paymentRails does not expose owner
│   └── it should revert with CowSwapModuleFactory_OwnerLookupFailed
├── when paymentRails returns malformed owner data
│   └── it should revert with CowSwapModuleFactory_OwnerLookupFailed
├── when paymentRails returns an owner word with dirty upper bits
│   └── it should revert with CowSwapModuleFactory_OwnerLookupFailed
├── when the caller is not the paymentRails owner
│   ├── it should revert with CowSwapModuleFactory_CallerNotPaymentRailsOwner
│   ├── it should revert for an attacker planting an attacker-owned module
│   ├── it should leave the victim paymentRails lookup empty
│   └── it should revert for the pending owner of an in-flight transfer
├── when the caller is the paymentRails owner
│   ├── it should deploy a new CowSwapModule contract
│   ├── it should set the owner on the deployed module
│   ├── it should allow a module owner different from the paymentRails owner
│   ├── it should wire the module to the PaymentRails
│   ├── it should wire the module to the factory chain config
│   ├── it should register the module in the factory
│   ├── it should increment the module count
│   ├── it should register the module under the PaymentRails lookup
│   ├── it should emit a CowSwapModuleCreated event
│   └── when called multiple times
│       ├── it should deploy distinct instances
│       ├── it should register all instances
│       └── it should accumulate instances in the PaymentRails lookup
└── when ownership of the paymentRails is transferred
    ├── it should reject the previous owner
    └── it should accept the new owner
